 new type of  undergarment for women that's was in  between traditional underwear that we  had to choose from and the heavy-duty  shapers girdles Nemer nine fail growing  up my dad used to encourage my brother  and me to fail and he would ask us at  the dinner table what we had failed at  that week and if we didn't have  something to tell him he would actually  be disappointed and I didn't realize it  at the time but he was just redefining  failure for me failure became about not  try  not the outcome going through life the  only failure that I ever feel that I've  had is if I don't try so that was a real  gift that he gave me and rule number 10  the last 24 very special bonus clip is  grow organically  I just wanted Oprah I had this product I  felt that it was a you know I was on to  something I needed to build a team I  needed some help so my boyfriend who was  the health care consultant he left his  job and he started helping me do all the  fulfillment  he said you got you you know I'd  semi-trucks pulling up twice a week to  my apartment in Atlanta and I was doing  all the shipping at night and he really  started helping me do the fulfillment  and we were in the back room we ended I  ended up starting the headquarters in my  best friend's bedroom she had moved out  and I we set up two cardboard tables in  the beginning and people used to call  and say I need to speak to shipping and  handling and we'd always say please hold  buy transfer you  then I then I then I went for a walk  with a friend to get a bagel and I'd  given her one of my prototypes and the  entire walk to get the bagel she all she  did was tell me how much she loved it by  the end of the walk I looked at her and  I said do you want to be my head of PR  she's like well I don't know anything  about PR I go I don't either I've been  calling these radio stations and  magazines and circling people's names  and newspapers and I think you could do  it just as good as I could if not better  you seem to really love the product so  she immediately came on board and  started doing that and then the third  person that joined my team was someone  that I was looking for an assistant  because at that time I was doing  everything and also trying to coordinate  my travel and it just got so crazy so  quickly so this woman Joo didya who had  been an interior designer came on board  to be my assistant and after two weeks  in my apartment I came home one day and  I looked at her and I said do you want  to be my head of product development she  looked at me she goes I don't know  anything about pantyhose or shapers I go  I don't either it's perfect now I've got  a special bonus clip from Sara that I  think you're going to enjoy but before  that it's time for the three point  landing questions let's go from just  watching the video to take an action  here we go question number one what gold  can you spend the next three minutes  visualizing it working number two where  can you be more vulnerable in your  business and number three what can you  do daily to help you believe in your  idea and if you like this video and will  take action after watching it give me a  hashtag believe down the comments as  well what keeps you so unbelievably  grounded amid all your resounding  success I I feel like success just makes  you more of who you already were I feel  like money and success just does that so  it's like it holds a magnifying glass up  to who you are people you know people  always ask you that and I'm like I don't  know who else to be I mean I am Who I am  so the money the success and so I like  to say if you were a jerk before you got  really successful and a lot of money you  should you become a bigger jerk usually  and if  you were insecure you'll become more  insecure if you were nice should become  nicer if you were generous should become  more generous it's literally just a  magnifying glass  if you want 10 more rules from sera  check out the last top 10 I made on her  the link is right there next to me I  think you'll enjoy it continue to  believe and I'll see you there  and I'm a terrible test taker after I  basically bombed the LSAT I hate tried  out at Disney World to be goofy  [Music]
 

